//? Title: FP-growth: actual prefix trees and weighted conditional patterns
//? Subtitle: Preserve the original groceries, inspect Titanic baskets and count the work behind compact trees
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
FP-growth aggregates shared transaction prefixes and extends frequent patterns
through weighted conditional databases. A four-basket example makes every node
and count checkable. Owned native traces then replace the original grocery
report's hand-drawn schematic with its actual tree and conditional paths.
On Titanic passenger attributes, the three native miners agree at a positive
threshold. Dense and disjoint controls show why a small initial tree can still
have exponentially many answers. Actual work and online history admission keep
compression, output size and memory limits distinct.
)

\toc

> Four baskets, three frequent sets

Take baskets {bread,milk}, {bread,milk}, {bread} and {milk}, with minimum count two.
Each singleton occurs in three rows; their pair occurs in two. Baskets are sets,
so repeated IDs inside one row count once, while repeated rows remain separate
observations. Empty rows also retain their identities. The native miner sorts
frequent items by support descending, breaking ties by ascending numeric ID.
Bread0 therefore precedes milk1 in this example.

The first two baskets share the path bread→milk; the third increments bread;
the last creates a separate milk node at the root. The following diagram uses
the actual created nodes, counts and parent indices. Its coordinates come from
the reusable native rooted-tree drawing method, rather than a hand-coded layout.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fp_growth_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/fp_growth.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/eclat.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <numeric>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::vector<std::size_t>> rows{{0,1},{0,1},{0},{1}};const std::vector<std::string> names{"bread","milk"};const auto t=dm::algorithms::fp_growth_trace(rows,2,38);
  std::print("| frequent set | support |\n| --- | ---: |\n");for(const auto&f:t.itemsets)std::print("| {} | {} |\n",dm::algorithms::itemset_label(f.items,names),f.support);
  std::print("\n| header item | actual node indices | summed support |\n| --- | --- | ---: |\n");for(const auto&h:t.trees[0].header){std::size_t total=0;for(auto id:h.nodes)total+=t.trees[0].nodes[id].count;std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",names[h.item],h.nodes,total);}
  const auto&pair=t.steps.at(1);std::print("\nMilk step: actual pattern {}; conditional path {} with weight {}; child tree {}; pair emitted as {} with support {}.\n",pair.pattern,pair.base.at(0).items,pair.base[0].weight,pair.child,t.steps.at(2).pattern,t.steps[2].support);
  std::vector<std::size_t> parents;std::vector<std::string> labels;for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.trees[0].nodes.size();++i){const auto&n=t.trees[0].nodes[i];parents.push_back(n.parent);labels.push_back(i?std::format("n{} {}\ncount{}",i,names[n.item],n.count):"n0 root");}
  dm::graphics::Diagram::rooted_tree(parents,labels,"Actual tiny FP-tree; minimum count2").save_svg("build/fp_growth_tiny.svg");
  if(t.itemsets.size()!=3||t.captured_entries!=38||pair.base[0].weight!=2)throw std::runtime_error("tiny weighted prefix control");
}
