\caption(The actual original tree has ten nonroot nodes. Diapers’ conditional base contains beer with weight two and beer,bread with weight one; beer survives at three, while conditional bread count one is pruned.)
\alttext(A native rooted tree draws every original grocery prefix with its actual node index and count: bread five, root milk one and root beer two, with their shared descendant paths.)

Beer accompanies diapers in all three relevant baskets, but that is not the
entire conditional base: bread also appears in one of its weighted paths. Its
conditional support one falls below two, leaving only beer at count three.
The base must preserve the target-specific weights even when prefixes are shared.

> Passenger baskets from the canonical Titanic table

Use all891 rows of the built-in Titanic table, selecting Pclass, Sex and Survived.
The native encoder creates one column=value item for each non-null selected cell;
repeated passengers with the same selected attributes remain separate rows.
The encoded rows contain2,673 unique incidences over seven observed items.
At minimum count45, all seven singletons survive and the three miners agree on
32 sets: seven singletons, sixteen pairs and nine triples.

The initial FP-tree uses23 nonroot nodes; all conditional builds together create58.
Those are structural counts, not byte savings or timing results. Attribute
combinations describe this table; support alone does not establish causation or a
predictive rule. The trace and figures are computed from the canonical dataset,
with no separately supplied data file.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fp_growth_titanic.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/fp_growth.hpp>
