\caption(The tiny history fits exactly38 retained entries and rejects37. Full-width item IDs remain distinct from the dummy root by node index. The bars expose the preserved zero-threshold API difference, rather than claiming universal three-miner equivalence.)
\alttext(A native bar chart shows two returned itemsets for FP-growth and three each for Apriori and Eclat on the disjoint baskets {0} and {1} at threshold zero.)

The trace captures these states in the same executing kernel, with no replay.
The trace owns raw rows, nodes, headers, emitted sequences and conditional paths.
Caller edits cannot change those records. The ordinary result and work-only API
use the same executing kernel without retaining this history or imposing its
optional quota. Captured raw inputs preserve duplicates; mining still counts
each item once per row. Opaque SIZE_MAX item IDs remain valid because only node
index zero denotes the root.

Every figure is regenerated by the complete native C++ program beside it. The
canonical passenger table is the only real dataset used; the tiny, grocery,
dense and disjoint controls have explicitly constructed inputs.
